{"type":"assistant","message":{"id":"chatcmpl-25e144be-32b2-4ee2-8a3c-a6615042ced7","type":"message","role":"assistant","model":"Claude-Opus-4.8","content":[{"type":"tool_use","id":"toolu_01BVHosDsGcDdKygyokyAEEW","name":"Bash","input":{"command":"python3 - <<'EOF'\nwls = [\n (\"W1\", 39, 7140, 97, 399096),\n (\"W2\", 4, 123, 12, 135698),\n (\"W3\", 29, 13515, 28, 2),\n (\"W4\", 2, 16384, 3, 25634),\n (\"W5\", 11, 4950, 25, 296392),\n]\nbw = 2039e9  # A800 HBM ~2 TB/s\nprint(f\"{'wl':>3} {'seqs':>5} {'q/seq':>7} {'kv/seq':>7} {'out_MB':>8} {'lse_MB':>7} {'floor_us':>9}\")\nfor n, li, tq, nkv, npg in wls:\n    seqs = li-1\n    out_b = tq*32*128*2\n    lse_b = tq*32*4\n    floor = (out_b+lse_b)/bw*1e6\n    print(f\"{n:>3} {seqs:>5} {tq/seqs:>7.1f} {nkv/seqs:>7.2f} {out_b/1e6:>8.1f} {lse_b/1e6:>7.2f} {floor:>9.1f}\")\nEOF","description":"Compute per-workload bandwidth floors"}}],"stop_reason":null,"stop_sequence":null,"usage":{"input_tokens":13951,"cache_creation_input_tokens":0,"cache_read_input_tokens":4871,"output_tokens":0},"context_management":null},"parent_tool_use_id":null,"session_id":"c1f2131a-03f6-47b7-8446-e27bd5e2211f","uuid":"64a90a35-6478-4739-b473-14021e009ac0","timestamp":"2026-09-16T13:51:25.855Z"}
